        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug arises from the incorrect handling of metadata on the ECPF (Embedded Control Plane Function) vport, where metadata was being enabled on the eswitch manager vport instead of the own vport. This led to traffic tagged by ingress ACL not being processed correctly at the NIC RX flow table level, as the metadata tag was not being utilized properly. The fix involves ensuring that operations are performed on the own vport to correctly pass metadata.

        Commit message:
        net/mlx5: E-switch, Enable metadata on own vport

Currently on ECPF, metadata is enabled on the ECPF vport = 0xfffe
(manager vport).
Metadata when supported, must be enabled on own vport which is
used to pass metadata to vport of NIC Rx Flow Table.

